## Context

Phase 3 is the HITL memory substrate that ticket 0102
(escalation-rate decay) depends on. Once an operator ratifies an
adjudication verdict (from Phase 2), that ruling is stored in
persistent memory so future runs on matching situations are
deterministic (tier-1) rather than escalating (tier-2/3).

Post-conference work. Do not start before 0118 is closed.

## Actions

1. Design the memory schema: keyed by (cell-type, source-domain,
   value-range) or similar; stores ratification verdict + timestamp
   + operator ID.
2. Wire into the fusion pipeline: before escalating a cell, check
   memory; if a match exists, apply the ratified verdict directly.
3. Provide a HITL ratification CLI: `scripts/verify/ratify.py`
   presents unratified Phase-2 verdicts for operator confirmation.
4. Run the fusion pipeline 3+ times over the Vietnam corpus with
   accumulating memory. Record escalation rates per run (feeds 0102).

## Exit criteria

- Memory schema + ratification CLI with tests.
- Pipeline reads memory before escalating.
- At least 3 accumulated runs logged (needed by 0102 for decay curve).
- 0102 unblocked.
